// CROWN refinement (P0, 2026-10-01): a function with a guarded precondition
// handed to a caller that will call it with values nothing proves — `apply`
// names no refinement on its callback's parameter, so the crossing carries
// the demand as debt, and the trap that demand guards is the crossing's to
// charge. Expect E_EffectMismatch at main.
type Positive = Int where 0 < self

fn inv(n: Positive) = 100 / n

fn apply(f, x) = f(x)

fn main() with !Trap = apply(inv, 0)
